{% comment %}
  Which collection should represent this product?

  The PDP breadcrumb used product.collections.first, which is Shopify's ordering —
  arbitrary, and not a statement about which parent means more. A product sitting in
  both Vitamins and Skin, Hair & Nails could breadcrumb to either, depending on
  nothing the merchant controls or intends.

  Both parents are true. The leaf is the more useful one: "Home / Skin, Hair & Nails"
  tells a visitor where they are, "Home / Vitamins" tells them the department they
  could already see in the nav.

  Ranks come from snippets/collection-rank.liquid, generated from the same taxonomy
  as the category breadcrumbs, so this cannot drift from the site's own structure:

    leaf at depth 3   7      most specific
    beauty-accessories 6
    leaf at depth 2   5
    group at depth 2  4
    menu at depth 1   2
    brand             1      a facet, not a taxonomy parent — last resort
    unknown           0

  Ties keep the earlier collection, so the result is stable rather than depending on
  iteration order for two equally specific parents.

  Brands rank last deliberately. "Home / Nurofen / Nurofen Plus" is a worse trail
  than "Home / Pain Relief / Nurofen Plus" — but it still beats no trail at all,
  which is why brands score 1 and not 0.

  Returns the chosen collection's HANDLE, or nothing when the product is in no
  collection. The caller resolves it back to the object; a snippet cannot return one.

  Usage:
    {%- capture primary %}{% render 'product-primary-collection', product: product %}{% endcapture -%}
    {%- assign primary = primary | strip -%}

  Accepts: product (required)
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign best_handle = ''
  assign best_rank = -1

  for c in product.collections
    capture rank_raw
      render 'collection-rank', handle: c.handle
    endcapture
    assign rank = rank_raw | strip | plus: 0

    if rank > best_rank
      assign best_rank = rank
      assign best_handle = c.handle
    endif
  endfor

  echo best_handle
-%}
